{
  "kanji": "倒",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 倒\ntitle: topple; collapse\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 人\nradicalNumber: 9\nonyomi: [トウ]\nkunyomi: [たお.れる, -だお.れ, たお.す, さかさま, さかさ, さかしま]\ndistractors: [例, 側, 借]\n---\n\n# 倒 — topple; collapse\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 人 (as 亻, no. 9) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n倒 is useful for something losing its upright position.\n[倒れる](../words/倒れる.md) たおれる describes something falling over; 倒す たおす describes bringing it down.\n転倒 てんとう names a fall or toppling.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the person on the left leaning toward the densely packed right side and losing balance.\nThe right side has the visible shape [到](到.md); no phonetic role is established here.\nThe story is a memory aid, not an origin claim.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| たお.れる | kun | [倒れる](../words/倒れる.md) たおれる — fall over |\n| たお.す | kun | 倒す たおす — knock over |\n| トウ | on | 転倒 てんとう — falling down |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [倒れる](../words/倒れる.md) たおれる — topple; collapse\n- 倒す たおす — bring down; knock over\n- 転倒 てんとう — a fall; toppling\n\n## Notes\n\nCompare 木が倒れる (きがたおれる), \"a tree falls over,\" with 木を倒す (きをたおす), \"fell a tree.\"\nThe radical 人 appears as 亻.\n[例](例.md) and [側](側.md) have similar outer components but different centers; [借](借.md) has a different right side altogether.\nNot every English use of \"fall\" is expressed with 倒れる.\n",
